          "title": "You'll want to know: ઘરેણું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઘરેણું — ghareṇũ — \"ornament, piece of jewellery\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દાદી પાસે જૂનું ઘરેણું છે. — dādī pāse jūnũ ghareṇũ che — \"Grandmother has an old piece of jewellery.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઘરેણું (ghareṇũ) is a tadbhava. CDIAL lists it, glossed \"jewelry\", under Sanskrit grahaṇa, \"seizing, holding\", in its second sense, \"putting on (clothes)\"; the same entry gives a Gujarati ghareṇe, \"in pawn\", under the first sense (CDIAL 4364)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
